      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The author reminds briefly the physiopathological basis of coronary circulation and points out the hydraulic factors as the most important for the maintenance of myocardial flow. That's the reason he shows the great actuality of the new therapies of acute and chronic coronary insufficiency (thrombolysis and angioplasty) fit for taking off the obstacles to anterograd flow."},
